' Observed behavior: accepted Skill startup failures stay on the existing ordinary stream.
' Observed behavior: typed requests and both real execution services already exist.
' Design reason: connect one public POST without duplicating normalization or execution lifecycle.
' Java divergence: structured JSON request, fail-closed errors, no local slash fallback.
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
title Shared command POST: JSON or ordinary message SSE
actor Client
participant "MVC / Request VO\n(request validation)" as MVC
participant "RuntimeCommandController\n(stateless singleton)" as Web
participant "CommandExecutionService\n(stateless singleton)" as Builtin
participant "Registry / Handler / Assembler\n(existing collaborators)" as Handlers
participant "SkillCommandExecutionService\n(stateless singleton)" as Skill
participant "Ordinary event execution\n(existing lifecycle)" as Events
participant "RuntimeExceptionHandler\n(stateless singleton)" as Errors
Client -> MVC: POST command: name, arguments, optional Skill files
MVC -> Web: Validated CommandRequestVO
Web -> Web: Reject forbidden headers by presence
alt Builtin request
  Web -> Builtin: executeBuiltinAndAwait
  Builtin -> Handlers: One catalog, admission, handler, VO projection
  Handlers --> Builtin: Isolated completion view
  Builtin -> Builtin: Await on request thread; unwrap failure
  Builtin --> Web: Business VO and optional ETag
  Web --> Client: 200 application/json, ResultBean
else Skill request
  Web -> Skill: executeRequest: map VO to DTO
  Skill -> Events: Existing normalization, actual binding, expanded message
  Events --> Web: Ordinary RuntimeEventStream
  Web --> Client: SseEmitter: ordinary domain events
  Client -> Web: Disconnect
  Web -> Events: Detach subscriber only
end
group Validation failure or application call throws before response
  MVC -> Errors: Binding or method validation failure
  Web -> Errors: Application failure
  Errors --> Client: Stable HTTP status and JSON error
end
note over Web,Events
No command lifecycle storage or public command id.
Accepted execution is not cancelled by client disconnect.
end note
@enduml
